LICENSE PENDING - OWNER DECISION REQUIRED
=========================================

This repository does NOT have an open-source license yet. This file is a placeholder and is
not itself a license.

Current legal position
----------------------
Until the repository owner chooses and adds a license, the default copyright rules apply:
the authors keep all rights, and nobody may copy, modify, distribute or build on this code,
except for what GitHub's Terms of Service allow (viewing and forking the repository on
GitHub). The root package.json declares "license": "UNLICENSED" for the same reason.

Recommendation (a suggestion, not legal advice)
-----------------------------------------------
Pick one of these two permissive licenses:

  * Apache-2.0 - preferred for this project. It is permissive, and it adds an explicit patent
    grant from every contributor plus a patent-retaliation clause. That matters for a project
    that others (including companies) may build on or contribute to, and it keeps the
    contributor terms unambiguous.

  * MIT - choose it if maximum simplicity and the shortest possible text matter more than an
    explicit patent grant. It is permissive and widely understood, but silent on patents.

Whichever you choose, do it deliberately: this file intentionally does not pick one for you.

To finish
---------
1. Replace this file with the full, unmodified text of the chosen license (for example from
   https://choosealicense.com/), with the copyright year and holder filled in.
2. Change "license" in package.json from "UNLICENSED" to the SPDX identifier (for example
   "Apache-2.0" or "MIT") and remove the "private" flag only if you intend to publish packages.
3. Update the "License" section of CONTRIBUTING.md and, if you want pull requests checked
   against a license allow-list, set allow-licenses in .github/workflows/dependency-review.yml.
4. Check that every dependency's license is compatible with your choice (third-party
   licenses are unaffected by this decision).
